@startuml tropical-semiring-algebra
' D17 — Tropical semiring algebra panel.
' Depicts: the (min, +) algebra duallity computes in, its two identities, and the consequence that
' a shortest path is the best answer.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #34495E
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}
title D17 · The tropical (min, +) semiring  𝕂 = (ℝ ∪ {+∞}, min, +, +∞, 0)

rectangle "<b>⊕  =  min</b>\nthe best (cheapest)\nalternative wins\n\nexample:  2 ⊕ 5 = 2" as PLUS #FCF3CF
rectangle "<b>⊗  =  +</b>\ncosts add up\nalong a path\n\nexample:  2 ⊗ 5 = 7" as TIMES #FCF3CF
rectangle "<b>0̄  =  +∞</b>\nidentity for ⊕\n(no path / forbidden)\n\nTropicalWeight::zero()" as ZERO #F2F3F4
rectangle "<b>1̄  =  0</b>\nidentity for ⊗\n(a free step)\n\nTropicalWeight::one()" as ONE #F9E79F

PLUS -[hidden]right- TIMES
ZERO -[hidden]right- ONE
PLUS -[hidden]down- ZERO
TIMES -[hidden]down- ONE

note bottom
  Under (min, +):  "⊕-sum over all paths" becomes "<b>minimum-cost path</b>",
  and "⊗-product along a path" becomes "<b>sum of edge costs</b>".
  So a shortest path <b>is</b> the best correction.
  ⚠ Note the naming: <b>zero()</b> is the value <b>+∞</b> and <b>one()</b> is the value <b>0</b>.
end note
@enduml
